WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.233
Small and medium businesses make up around ninety percent of businesses worldwide.

2
00:00:05.233 --> 00:00:10.700
But limited expertise, competing sustainability frameworks and different buyer expectations

3
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:13.767
leave many asking: where should we start?

4
00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:19.100
Created by Columbia sustainability management students,

5
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.367
MOSAIC starts with a simple idea:

6
00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:27.567
what matters depends on your buyers, markets, location, industry, size and goals.

7
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.667
It starts with a selected knowledge base.

8
00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:33.267
AI extracts and tags individual indicators.

9
00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:38.900
The system connects related requirements within documents and across the collection.

10
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:43.600
Recurrence informs each question’s base weight.

11
00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:48.833
Context multipliers adjust that question’s relevance.

12
00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:54.633
Category weights set the emphasis across broader areas for the industry.

13
00:00:54.633 --> 00:00:56.867
These settings guide consistent scoring.

14
00:00:56.867 --> 00:00:57.567
Change the knowledge base,

15
00:00:57.567 --> 00:01:02.100
and the same engine can be configured for different markets, buyers or industries.

16
00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:08.300
Your profile selects relevant questions.

17
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.800
Your answers produce weighted results.

18
00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:19.167
AI interprets these alongside source evidence, explaining priorities and next steps.

19
00:01:19.167 --> 00:01:21.500
Buyers see data readiness and gaps.

20
00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:25.167
For small businesses, sustainability must make business sense.

21
00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:27.200
MOSAIC.

22
00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:30.000
The pieces that matter. A clearer way forward.
